  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1243 AM CST Sun Nov 22 2026\n\nA cold front is stretching from the upper Great Lakes down to \ncentral Oklahoma early this morning as an upper trough follow \nquickly behind. These features are progged to shift eastward through \nthe Quad State area today before exiting to the east of the area \nlate this evening. This will lead to a good chance (80-100%) of rain \nstarting across SEMO this morning, then spreading eastward through \nthe day. It will be a quick moving and fairly narrow band of \nrainfall, so it shouldn't last much more than 3 to 4 hours at any \nlocation once the rain starts. The quick movement will result in \naround a tenth to a quarter inch of rainfall for most locations. \nSome thunder is also possible, especially across portions of SEMO \ninto western KY as the front moves through during peak heating. In \nfact, up to 400 J/kg of instability is progged to build along\nand near the frontal boundary. Winds will become gusty from the\nnorth after the cold front passes, with gusts reaching as high \nas 30 mph this afternoon into this evening across SEMO into \nsouthern IL. \n\nDry Canadian high pressure will then build across the Quad State \nregion for Monday and Tuesday, allowing for chilly temperatures and \ndry weather for a couple of days. Highs will only be in the upper \n40s to around 50 degrees with lows in the low to mid 20s.\n\nThe next chance of rain arrives for Tuesday night into Wednesday as \nan upper low passes through the area, possibly even lingering into \nThursday with the latest guidance and ensemble data. In fact, it \nlooks like it may be just cold enough to allow a few snowflakes to \nmix in on the far northern edges of the precipitation. Not expecting \nany impacts from the snow showers, but roadways may end up being a \nlittle wet into Thanksgiving if the low linger longer.\n\nUnsettled weather may linger a bit longer as a trough lingers nearby \nand shortwave energy passes through the flow. Moisture looks to be \nlimited, but can't rule out some lingering cloud cover and possibly \nsome light precipitation into Friday and Saturday",
